diff --git a/reports/sign-det-encode-model.md b/reports/sign-det-encode-model.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..8da369877
--- /dev/null
+++ b/reports/sign-det-encode-model.md
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Exact graph encoding
+
+`Hex.SignDetBench.runEncode` uses mode 1, a two-sided parametric registration.
+It encodes the same supplied rational replay tree as the sparse-support family:
+P=X²−1, s identical queries X, and s=64,128,256,512,1024,2048. Preparation builds
+and checks the tree and an independent fixture-specific graph outside timing.
+The timed body runs the general `Dag.encode` and compares its entire literal
+entry array and root index against that graph. The required result is `true`.
+
+The full tree has 2s−1 occurrences. Hash consing visits each occurrence;
+hashing an arity-k entry and comparing an exact repeat each scan Θ(k) slots
+of bounded-size coefficients, matrix entries and polynomial witnesses. Local
+indices fit one machine word throughout the schedule. The distinct nodes have
+arities 1,2,4,…,s and at most four columns. The sum of input arities
+over the balanced tree is s(log₂s+1), yielding the declared Θ(s log s) model
+under the hash table's expected constant bucket work. The final exact output
+comparison scans the graph's 2s−1 arity volume, adding Θ(s). Hash collisions
+still compare all literal fields, as tested by the conformance fixtures;
+the model does not promise constant-time adversarial collision handling.
+
+The six fixed trial-major rounds use the existing lean-bench registration,
+an automatically leased CPU and no host-idleness filter. Every completed
+sample and any inconclusive verdict are retained. The runner's `--encoding`
+option selects this schedule without rerunning the previously measured tree,
+graph, producer or component schedules. At most one unchanged rerun is allowed
+after an inconclusive result, with both runs retained.
+
+This measures general encoding plus exact output equality, not graph replay,
+query production, byte serialization or coefficient-proof graph construction.
+It makes no paired speedup claim against the fixture encoder or the tree
+checker. Peak RSS includes preparation and is not encoder allocation. Growing
+support, coefficient/witness bits, extension levels and nested evidence remain
+separate Phase-4 requirements. The generic forward round-trip proof is
+`Dag.replay_encode`; this benchmark is not a substitute for that proof or the
+root-level semantic foundations.
+
+## Recorded observations
+
+The clean source revision `5329cec59c5bfb4a50a72a2bcfa82bb7ffb07da7`
+completed all 36 declared samples on `chungus2`, using automatically leased
+logical CPU 88. Every sample returned the expected hash of `true`, confirming
+exact equality with the independently constructed graph. No completed sample
+was discarded and no rerun was used. The harness reports
+`consistent_with_declared_complexity`, normalized slope −0.027712, with no
+advisories. This is evidence for the declared family model, not a worst-case
+hash-table bound.
+
+| Queries | Median milliseconds | Sample range in milliseconds |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 64 | 0.519 | 0.517–0.651 |
+| 128 | 1.097 | 1.091–1.109 |
+| 256 | 2.254 | 2.248–2.263 |
+| 512 | 4.627 | 4.385–4.738 |
+| 1024 | 9.775 | 9.536–10.503 |
+| 2048 | 25.397 | 23.998–29.518 |
+
+The [raw export](data/sign-det-encode/5329cec59/runEncode.json) retains all
+per-call times, inner repeat counts, result hashes and complete process RSS.
+`alloc_bytes` is unavailable; no encoder allocation measurement is claimed.
+The [metadata](data/sign-det-encode/5329cec59/metadata.json) records the exact
+commands, executable and source hashes, host context, harness revision and
+source archive. Reconstructing that archive against the recorded merged base
+verified every source hash before measurement. The inventory, logs and all
+completed observations are retained alongside the export. These timings are
